26	2	2	TT-210718 - Denise Navarro ( CPE is 10.77.15.38 up,   AP looks to be offline )    	&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;Denise actually called in reported downd internet Saturday at 6pm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;cpe-Denise.Navarro&amp;nbsp;10.77.15.38&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;br style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;We did not turn on *2886 when we left on saturday.&amp;nbsp; I found her message in support vm's.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;logged into cpe and so it appears that their Access Point ( 10.0.253.10 )&amp;nbsp; is offline.&amp;nbsp; Calling Her son Alanzo [&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;(707) 843-9784 ]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;around 3pm sunday July 18th to walk him through getting the access point back up&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, &amp;quot;Trebuchet MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 13px;"&gt;_______________________________________________&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;Talked to both Denise and Her Son.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;He tried both unplugging it and hitting the reset button.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;She is out of town because&amp;nbsp;her mom is not doing well.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Her son might stay there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;Will touch base with them tomorrow and schedule a time to go out there.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;Kevin ( 7/18/2021 )&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;_______________________________________________&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;Fix;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Andres logged into the defaulted WAP remotely&amp;nbsp;and reconfigured it. Denise's son factory reset&amp;nbsp;the WAP during the 7/16/2021 Friday&amp;nbsp;outage.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Added the alias 192.168.1.2 to eth0 on the CPE and then was able to ping the OpenWRT default IP of 192.168.1.1 on the puck. Then we proxy'ed into the CPE and remotely&amp;nbsp;configured the puck to original settings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;UAP-AC-LR OpenWRT 10.0.253.10 (NavarroNet /&amp;nbsp; 7079757760)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;No charge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color="#333333" face="sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, Trebuchet MS"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px;"&gt;-JM 07.20.2021&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1834	3	2021-07-18	\N	\N	2021-07-18 13:22:23.212604-07	\N	2021-07-20 13:57:32.024456-07	James	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
25	4	2	SysOpts-200717 - H20-AP LTU Upgrade	&lt;p&gt;Ian | Kevin&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Project:&amp;nbsp; H20-Relay Radio Update.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; (&amp;nbsp; Testing out&amp;nbsp; Ubnt&amp;nbsp; LTU&amp;nbsp; line) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Scheduled:&amp;nbsp; sunday 12:30 - 1 am&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; w/ kevin / Ian&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.)&amp;nbsp; Test new ap&amp;nbsp; and Swap customers over from the existing PrismStation5 AC over to the new radio.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; a.)&amp;nbsp; reconfigure the newly installed Rocket-PrismStation5 AC w/ 90 degree sector.&amp;nbsp; To match North most (sector radio 10.77.16.152)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;000.)&amp;nbsp; Assign this to Andre/James&lt;/u&gt;-----&amp;nbsp; A.)&amp;nbsp; Need to do a power&amp;nbsp; measurement on the LTU-AP.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;( would like to see what the baseline power requirement is for it.&amp;nbsp; So we can calculate it in the battery back up calcs.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.)&amp;nbsp; Look at the cpe's before and look at signal strengths and data rates.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Then do the same on after we move them over to the temporary AP( Temp.AP10.77.16.152 )&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3.)&amp;nbsp; Figure a plan based on worse looking signal strengh and if someone is actually having issues.&amp;nbsp; Then we'll need to move things back and upon setting up the LTU,&amp;nbsp; we'll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; a.) arrange to replace them first.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4.)&amp;nbsp; Must put avaram in the loop here as well.&amp;nbsp; He has been emailing me when is this going to happen?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; a.)&amp;nbsp; was thinking we could set him up in a dual-cpe configuration.&amp;nbsp; He has a cinder-block with a NSM5.&amp;nbsp; we could power it up while also switch out to a NSM5AC model as well to get gigbit ethernet ports too.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ian, at 1am on 7/19.2021 configured the new ap to match and were able to connect all 20 clients.&amp;nbsp; Some actually improved their signal strength.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We left all clients connected to the Prismstation5AC and so we can begin to migrate clients to the LTU. j&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kevin&amp;nbsp; 7.19.2021&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_______________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon review of ticket, items on this list have been completed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-JM 08/31/21&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1705	9	2021-07-19	3	\N	2021-07-17 16:54:40.106156-07	\N	2021-08-31 16:50:27.910964-07	James	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
