="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;990&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;6,650&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- MS (10-24-18)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Service Call Performed on 10-25-18&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.) (7.5) Hours Labor (@ $90 p/hour) (Two Man Labor) = &lt;b&gt;$675&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;2.) (2) NBe5AC-19 (@ $120 ea) = &lt;b&gt;$240&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;3.) (1) Netonix WS-6-mini (@ $175 ea.) = &lt;b&gt;$175&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note1: Ran conduit (almost) to lower fencepost near oak. Set up PTP from lower project to utility shed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note2: Need cantex box for utility shed (house Netonix)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;1,090&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;7,740&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- MS (10-25-18)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Service Call Performed on 10-26-18&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.) (6) Hours Labor (@ $90 p/hour) (Two Man Labor) = &lt;b&gt;$540&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;2.) (1) Cantex (@ $50 ea.) = &lt;b&gt;$50&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note: Got lower cam. cable run w. weatherhead. Conduit to post (fire rd cam and cam on upper ridge)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $ 590&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;8,330&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- MS (10-26-18)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Service Call Performed on 11-7-18&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.) (4) Hours Labor (@ $90 p/hour) (Two Man Labor) = &lt;b&gt;$360&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note: Got cable pulled at lower garden, for AP and cameras&lt;br&gt;Note: Also worked on conduit at upper garden (non-billable infrastructure)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $ 360&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;8,690&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- MS (11-7-18)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: rgb(255, 0, 0);"&gt;Running Parts Summary (non-electronic items) = &lt;b&gt;$757.89&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Running Total =&amp;nbsp;9,448&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;______________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;SCHEDULED RADIO SWAP &amp;amp; SITE SURVEY/EVALUATION:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TUE - 09.24.2019 @ 12pm - onwards&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Radio swap for Greg Windisch&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Pat.B Project Site Survey/Evaluation&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;• Get in touch with Pat or Randall&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;• Survey upper garden/home:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ Confirm Tent location.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ Confirm Trench locations&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ Confirm any other changes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;• Survey lower garden&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ Confirm and check boxes and cabling&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ Confirm Peeler Core&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ○ confirm if there another cable for the camera by the gate&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Survey gate/shed area&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Confirm Location for Cameras.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Inform Pat/Randall about moving the cameras higher from the current location as an option.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Alternative Locaion for 2.4 Radio in Dead tree&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**Rhinobee Team Please Update this ticket Thoroughly**&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;AL -09.24.2019&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bill for truck roll survey: &lt;b&gt;$110&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $ 110&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;9,558&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;SCHEDULED ONSITE WORK:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;THU 09.26.2019 @ 9AM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gate and Shed Area&lt;br&gt;* Placing down pole at gate and installing/mounting a camera and a NSM900 to shoot to the gate&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* replacing and remounting the cameras at the shed&lt;br&gt;* placing the netonix in a cantex box&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lower garden&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* installing/mounting the camera by the gate&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br class="Apple-interchange-newline"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outline of the job on the 26th of September, 2019&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Surveyed the area allowing Andre a better understanding of the project.&lt;br&gt;* Got into contact with Pat and with his help fleshed out the project and key areas:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Gate&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Shed&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Lower garden&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Upper Garden&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Upper Back Garden&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;* Installed 2 Bullet ICRealTime Cameras and 1 NSM900 Radio, Currently Unpowered&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;List of Billable Items:&lt;br&gt;* (1) NanoStation M900 (@120/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$120&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (2)&amp;nbsp;IC Realtime&amp;nbsp;Bullet Cameras (175/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$350&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (2) Weather Proof Boxes (25/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$50&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (2) Mounts (25/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$50&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* &lt;span style="background-color: rgb(255, 0, 0);"&gt;(1) 8' Cantex Box (50/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$50&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (2.75) Hours of labor - Rich @ 110.00/hr = &lt;b&gt;$302.50&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (2.75) Hours of labor - Andre @ 110.00/hr = &lt;b&gt;$302.50&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;1,225&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;10,783&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;AL - 9.30.2019&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;SCHEDULED INSTALLATION:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TUE-10.01.2019 @ 8AM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* House/Basement&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Swapping out the 8 port ICRealTime NVR for the 16 port ICRealTime NVR&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Shed:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Powering up Cameras and NSM900&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Configuring Cameras and Radio&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Taking Down Old Cameras&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Placing Netonix and cables in Cantex (clean-up)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Providing a POE Brick for the Bunny Ears UniFi&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Gate:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Flex conduit with Ethernet cables&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Camera&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • NSM900 pointing to Shed&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Cameras and Radios (after the Shed)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Lower Garden:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Installing and powering camera pointing down Road to shed and Camp Area.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Installing and powering camera pointing up the Garden.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Misc Jobs:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Testing Bullet Cameras vs Dome Cameras&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Scouting a Location for another Point-to-Point at the lower Garden to eliminate devices and hops at the shed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Emailed and called Pat to let him know we'll be up there early 8am -9am.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Billing:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* (1) Netonix 12 Port = &lt;b&gt;$350&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (5.5) Hours of labor - Rich @ 110.00/hr = &lt;b&gt;$605&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (5.5) Hours of labor - Andre @ 110.00/hr =&lt;b&gt; $605&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* (1) IC Realtime Bullet Cameras (175/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$175&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;* Parts and Pieces = &lt;b&gt;$100&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;TOTAL = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;1,835&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Running Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;12,618&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Need to find final billing details for job on 10.01.2019 to finalize old pat bransford ticket&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;Grand Total = $&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;12,618&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-AL 3.11.2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I have sent invoice #38840. Though due to the size of this bill I will be keeping this ticket open and keeping tabs on this invoice till I confirm payment has been made.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;- JD 4/22/22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Passing this ticket on to Linda to watch over as she handles billing now.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 7/6/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Billed customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-LRK 8/29/22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1050	12	2022-03-14	2	\N	2022-03-11 17:20:22.679366-08	Andre	2022-08-29 13:13:33.34681-07	Linda	\N	\