3	8	2	TT-210711 - Kelly Parsons - ()	&lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kelly Parsons:&amp;nbsp; Lan issue&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.)&amp;nbsp; 3 computers can not get online&lt;br&gt;2.)&amp;nbsp; maybe add switch ( monitored version)&lt;br&gt;3.) 192.168.20.13 AP&amp;nbsp; can not be accessed,&amp;nbsp; replace both pucks with UNIFI controller version.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; with a NSM2 it does not pass traffic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;cpe-Parson.Homegrown = 10.77.4.37&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;CPE is on barn @ end of driveway, PoE brick &amp;amp; Linksys rtr in east-side corner room of barn&lt;br&gt;Has own 2.4 PTP devices beaming to house from barn.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jul 10th, 2021&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt; Weare, Kevin&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Kelley called in reporting her office computers cant access the internet&lt;br&gt;* Connected to her CPE and confirmed it had internet connection&lt;br&gt;* Logged into her LAN via socks proxy tunnel and connected to 192.168.20.10, .11, and .12, all were online.&lt;br&gt;* Had her try and ping 8.8.8.8 from office computer, 75% packet loss&lt;br&gt;* Confirmed office computer is connected to swith via eithernet cable.&lt;br&gt;* Power cycled the switch in the barn, tried to ping 8.8.8.8 from office computer but still seeing massive traffic loss.&lt;br&gt;* Reseated eithernet cable in computer and in wall, still seeing packet loss.&lt;br&gt;* Having Andre head out to the property monday 11am to check LAN on 7.12.2021.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-JM - 07.10.2021&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Follow up with Her and make sure everything is working fine.&amp;nbsp; Then talk about the bill.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Was the tomatoes a gift? [Yes]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kevin ( 7-16-2021 )&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two separate bills:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1) time putting in puck (2hrs)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2) second trip to put in netonix switchs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;--&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;From webcollab ticket:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Billing&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;* Kayla can you create separate bills for these two jobs. the one on march fell through the cracks where we added another Access Point to her main house. Today we were trouble shooting her network to get her back to business.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;1.) From previous job (03.23.2021) :&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;* (&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;) UniFi AP AC LR Access Point (@ $150/ea) =&lt;b&gt; $150&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;* (&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;) hours of labor (@ $110/hr) = &lt;b&gt;$220&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;2.) From Today (07.12.2021):&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;* (&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;) hours of labor (@ $110/hr) =&lt;b&gt; $220&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;* (&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;) Netonix 6 switches (@ $200/ea) =&lt;b&gt; $400&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;-AL 7.12.2021&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-left: 25px;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;-JM 7/21/21&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Emailed Invoice #35526 and #35527 on 9.3.2021&lt;/p&gt