297	4	2	SysOpts-220311 - mrtg1 (  unifi.rhinobee.com (100.64.1.188) [CPU Usage] )	&lt;p&gt;Ian,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.) can we expand the size of the processor to this vm?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.)&amp;nbsp; can we start adding processor status into zabbix?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://mrtg1.rhinobee.com/mrtg/meta/linux-boxes/unifi.rhinobee.com.html" target="_blank"&gt;http://mrtg1.rhinobee.com/mrtg/meta/linux-boxes/unifi.rhinobee.com.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h1 style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;"&gt;unifi.rhinobee.com (100.64.1.188) [CPU Usage]&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;The statistics were last updated Saturday, 12 March 2022 at 3:38,&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;at which time 'unifi.rhinobee.com' had been up for 48 days, 9:36:09.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;b&gt;`Daily' Graph (5 Minute Average)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;b&gt;day&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Max&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;Average&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;Current&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;b&gt;cpu:&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;100.0 % (100.0%)&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;68.0 % (68.0%)&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;74.0 % (74.0%)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Out&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;100.0 % (100.0%)&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;68.0 % (68.0%)&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;74.0 % (74.0%)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=""&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;Kevin 3/11/2022&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;_____________________________&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;* Successfully reduced UniFi VM's CPU usage (now averaging ~35% usage) by following some of the steps suggested in this doc:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005159588-UniFi-How-to-Tune-the-Network-Application-for-High-Number-of-UniFi-Devices#2" target="_blank"&gt;https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005159588-UniFi-How-to-Tune-the-Network-Application-for-High-Number-of-UniFi-Devices#2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005159588-UniFi-How-to-Tune-the-Network-Application-for-High-Number-of-UniFi-Devices#2" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1.) On 3/15/22: Doubled unifi VM's memory from 4GB to 8GB (by updating the VM's XML config on VM host 'sirius'), and then Increased UniFi controller software's memory allocation from 2GB to 4GB, per support doc instructions. Waited a few days to see the impact: the memory increase reduced CPU usage by about ~20%... a good start, but still too high, hitting ~80% at peaks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2.) On 3/21/22: Enabled high-performance Java Garbage Collector, and waited a few days to see the difference... Minimal difference from this change.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3.) On 3/27/22: Added a 2nd CPU core to unifi VM  (by updating the VM's XML config on VM host 'sirius', after first testing the change on currently-unused unifi-restore VM). This made the biggest difference... CPU usage now averaging ~35%, with only occasional spikes above 50%.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;* See my log entries from the dates listed^ for detailed notes on the configuration changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;* CPU usage looks good &amp;amp; stable after the changes above, so I'm closing this ticket.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;* We should still update the UniFi controller software sometime soonish (which would enable us to try the other suggested CPU-load reduction fix from the support doc, "Increase Mongo WiredTiger engine cache"). We can do that update on a VM clone (rather than the current production controller VM), but migrating all the UniFi sites/devices to over to the updated controller is still scary, as it will most likely re-provision ALL the devices at once.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;-IR 3/30/22&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;	\N	7	2022-03-15	4	\N	2022-03-12 03:48:56.208353-08	Kevin	2022-03-30 15:04:01.232117-07	Ian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
