319	2	2	TT-220328 DeDomenico.Arena (13424 Chalk Hill Rd Healdsburg)	&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Charlie Martin&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;(415) 265-4339&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;13424 Chalk Hill Rd Healdsburg, CA&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled visit 9-10am Tuesday 03/29/2022:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Wan't to examine the NVR and the wiring leading up to it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;DeDomenico.Arena NVR (10.77.81.59) has been down for a while.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Tried reaching out to Charlie and left a voice message. Waiting on a call back.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Charlie called back:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He went to check on it and nothing appears on, also no obvious sign of power source.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Need to schedule a visit, to check in on it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-Aaron 03/28/2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_______________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon visit Rich noticed that the van wasn't working so he brought back the NVR to the office.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We had Another NVR available so we swapped them out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rich went back out and installed the NVR.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Had to adopt the cameras to the new device.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Still need to Upgrade the NVR's firmware.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-Aaron&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Edit 4.1.2022 by Andre Lee: NVR's firmware has been updated and the Web-UI is working (10.77.81.60)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;* Billing:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* (2) Hours of Labor per Truck roll to the property (@ $125/hr) = &lt;b&gt;$250&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* (1) UniFi NVR (@ $400/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$400&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOTAL = $650&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-AL 4.1.2022&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Emailed invoice #38908&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;- JD 4/1/22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1769	10	2022-03-31	2	\N	2022-03-28 10:50:43.463622-07	Aaron	2022-04-01 17:37:22.290083-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
140	2	2	SR-210922 - Pat Bransford ( Rebuild - Pats- LAN  @ \t2260 Los Alamos Rd ) 	&lt;p&gt;Pat Bransford&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2260 Los Alamos Rd&lt;br&gt;Santa Rosa, CA 95409&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;pat@patbransford.com&lt;br&gt;(707) 481-1218&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Do not see any of the devices wirelessly connected to AP's&amp;nbsp; 9/28/2021 8:48am&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rebuild LAN and ExpandingWiFi Network&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Day 1:&amp;nbsp; Install radios - Thursday 09.23.2021&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;1.)&amp;nbsp; what was done?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;• A NanoStation M2 and a NanoStation 5AC were installed on the upper garden Corner&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 2.) how many hours of labor: &lt;b&gt;1.5 Hours&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 3.) what gear was installed:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;NanoStation M2 in SOHO Router Mode: 10.77.9.22 - Providing PoE-PT to the NanoStation 5AC&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;NanoStation 5AC 10.0.35.200&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Day 2:&amp;nbsp; Installed Non-Pens - Friday 09.24.2021&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 1.)&amp;nbsp; what was done?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;cat5 Cable was run from the Radios installed on the Upper Garden Corner to the Netonix 6 at BzP.S Relay to provide Power over Ethernet on Port 5.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • cat5 Cable was run from the old NanoBeam 5AC (10.0.35.201) to the Netonix 12 at BzP.N Relay to provide Power over Ethernet on Port 11.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • The Netonix12 at BzP.N has a vlan to separate the relay network from Pat's Network&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • NanoStation M2 (10.77.9.7) Has been configured to become a Bridged accesspoint (10.0.35.202)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Investigated and repaired the conduit run from the powerbox at BzP.N to a Wooden Pole&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Investigated the conduit run from the PowerBox at BzP.N to the weather-head under the NonPen for BzP.N - Cables have a hard time being pulled through: Temp solution - Run cable on the Ground.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Placed 2 non-pens to be placeholders for solar and provide power for the radios at the corner of the upper garden and the lower garden.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 2.) how many hours of labor: &lt;b&gt;3hours and 45 minutes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 3.) what gear was installed:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;Mgnt-net 10.0.35/24&amp;nbsp; ( used .200 and above to avoid having any of the old LAN-NET still in nagios report erroneously )&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://ibis.rhinobee.com/cgi-bin/nagios/extinfo.cgi?type=1&amp;amp;host=cpe-rtr.bransford.LAN.AP" title="10.77.9.22" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(73, 106, 239); text-decoration-line: underline;"&gt;cpe-rtr.bransford.LAN.AP&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;10.77.9.22&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://ibis.rhinobee.com/cgi-bin/nagios/extinfo.cgi?type=1&amp;amp;host=LAN-Brandsford-AP.BH-BzP.S-ptp-BzP.N" title="10.0.35.200" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(63, 91, 205); text-decoration-line: underline;"&gt;LAN-Brandsford-AP.BH-BzP.S-ptp-BzP.N&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; 10.0.35.200&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://ibis.rhinobee.com/cgi-bin/nagios/extinfo.cgi?type=1&amp;amp;host=LAN-Brandsford-ST.BH-BzP.N-ptp-BzP.S" title="10.0.35.201" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(26, 13, 171); font-family: arial, verdana, serif; font-size: 10.6667px;"&gt;LAN-Brandsford-ST.BH-BzP.N-ptp-BzP.S&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;10.0.35.201&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://ibis.rhinobee.com/cgi-bin/nagios/extinfo.cgi?type=1&amp;amp;host=LAN-Brandsford-BzP.N-AP.2" title="10.0.35.202" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(73, 106, 239); text-decoration-line: underline;"&gt;LAN-Brandsford-BzP.N-AP.2&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 10.0.35.202&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://ibis.rhinobee.com/cgi-bin/nagios/extinfo.cgi?type=1&amp;amp;host=LAN-Brandsford-AP.BH-BzP.N-ptp-BzP.LG" title="10.0.35.203" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(63, 91, 205); text-decoration-line: underline;"&gt;LAN-Brandsford-AP.BH-BzP.N-ptp-BzP.LG&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;10.0.35.203 ( Not Installed Yet&amp;nbsp; )&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Day 3:&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Emergency Maintenance and Repair at BzP.S Relay - Tuesday 09.28.2021&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 1.)&amp;nbsp; what was done?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp;nbsp;BzP South Emergency Repairs&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Summary:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; •&amp