513	2	2	TT-221025 - Brad Meyers (505 Kinnybrook Drive)	&lt;p&gt;Brad Meyer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;505 Kinnybrook Drive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kennybrook, CA 95452&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;b.meyer@dthrac.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(317) 557-2369&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;______________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Explained he has been in communication with Andre about poor connection on his property.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* He told me that the over all connection at the property is very sporadic.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* He said a lot of WiFi calls will drop.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Will need to look into network and check in with Andre about this issue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 10/25/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Checked in with Andre and he helped me look into the situation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Logged into his CPE and updated the firmware to the latest firmware, same with the access point at H2O.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Changed the modulation rate from 8x to 10x.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Signal strength is now looking better.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Though we are noticing the LTU Rocket only showing Kb's.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* We also noticed a lot of his charts on MRTG have suddenly flat lined with spikes here and there, Andre is having Ian look into it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Called Brad to have him run a test but he will call us back as hes busy with a zoom call.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 10/25/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled Service Call Configuring 10.25.2022 @ 9-10AM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Replacing LTU Station with a NanoBeam 5AC Radio (10.77.17.58) to connect to ap.kennybrook.H20 (10.77.16.52)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-AL 10.25.2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Recovered LTU-AP and a LTU CPE.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Swapped LTU CPE with the NanoBeam 5AC [10.77.17.58]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Sorted frequency issues at the gym that was causin