320	2	2	TT-220329 Kim Edwards (6238 Cottage Ridge Rd)	&lt;p&gt;Kim Edwards&lt;br&gt;(707) 326-5456&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6238 Cottage Ridge Rd Santa Rosa&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled visit 8am 03/30/2022&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are replacing the cpe and st&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-Aaron&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Test 1:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- Replaced the NanoStation 5AC configured to be the CPE/AP (10.77.2.46), station (10.77.2.49), and power supply&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- Rich tested uncapped results - 10 - 12Mbps DOWN / 5-8 Mbps UP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Test 2:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- Disabled dhcp reservation on cpe_Inf-AP.E-K.Edwards.Relay [10.77.2.46] to connect to Rich's laptop&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Rich tested uncapped results - 10 - 12Mbps DOWN / 5-8 Mbps UP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Test 3:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- Bypassed the Access Point by connecting directy to the BH-ST and changing the Network Role from Bridged mode to router mode.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Rich tested uncapped results - 10 - 12Mbps DOWN / 5-8 Mbps UP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Test 4:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- Changed access points&amp;nbsp; from&amp;nbsp;AP-3-RWH-5ghz [10.77.2.183] -&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;AP-2-RWH-5ghz [10.77.2.13]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Rich tested uncapped results - 15 - 18Mbps DOWN / 5-8 Mbps UP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Ultimately Changing the AMPDU Setting to 32 and Enabling the AMSDU setting fixed the issue of the Station causing an artificial bandwidth limit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Rich tested uncapped results on the BH-ST (10.77.2.49) - 70-75Mbps DOWN / 20-23 Mbps UP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-AL + AH 3.30.2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled Cable Replacement - From the NanoStation 5AC to the PoE Brick in the garage - 4.12.2022 @ 9-10AM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Mary Edwards had set this appointment up in advance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* This will be the last of the changes made to ensure that on our side, everything has been replaced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-AL 4.11.2022&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Billing:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Truck roll for replacing cable run and testing on his network.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(1) Hour of Labour (truck roll) (@ $125/hr) = &lt;b&gt;$125&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-AL 4.13.2022&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Emailed invoice #38912&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;- JD 4/14/22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1033	10	2022-04-12	2	\N	2022-03-29 18:41:06.646208-07	Aaron	2022-04-14 14:32:31.625887-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
