283	4	2	SysOpts-220302 -  xwiki - reinstall /  recovery ( Old Heffalump running Openbsd 6.1)  	&lt;p&gt;Project goal:&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;To try and install xwiki working on an OpenBSD 6.1 box and to see if we can restore the xwiki from Euclid ( also an OpenBSD 6.1 box that its harddrive failed )&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* we tried to do a disk to disk copy of the harddrive twice but it failed at 90% both times.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.)First lets try the former mrtg node old heffilump to see if we can restore it there first.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;APU board Old heffalump w/ Openbsd 6.1&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;( 100.64.1.130)&amp;nbsp; w/Harddrive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.) if that fails or too complicate on top of ed's wacko box of perl scripts and database weberery,&amp;nbsp; then lets install 6.1 on an APU and try from scratch to see if we can get it restored.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After thinking of this we also want to try and get Euclid dev 1.0 working on a 6.1 web server as well. so perhaps a brand new install would be preferred?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;VM?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(Kevin 3/2/2022)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;______________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Looked into installing xwiki on OpenBSD 6.1 (or cirrent OpenBSD release), but found that it's not in Packages, nor even in Ports. Discussed with Kevin, and decided to use Debian (the platform recommended by the Xwiki project for production installs).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Created new 'xwiki' Debian 11 VM on 'polaris' host, installed / configured Xwiki, following the official docs:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Installation/InstallationViaAPT/" target="_blank"&gt;https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Installation/InstallationViaAPT/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Tried (unsuccessfully) various methods of restoring old Xwiki content from Ed's old backup (postgresql dumps were backed up to nimbus/nombus), starting from the instructions from this doc:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Backup" target="_blank"&gt;https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Documentation/AdminGuide/Backup&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Postgresqll DB restore process finished without errors (and the new xwiki's database data directory grew in size as expected), but nothing I tried got the old content to show up on the new Xwiki pages. Read various forum posts, and purged/reinstalled the database &amp;amp; packages/dependencies to re-try with several alternate methods (see my log entries for detailed notes) but without success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Grep'd Ed's xwiki postgres dump file, and confirmed the wiki page \r\ncontents are there in plaintext, but without proper formatting, and \r\nhundreds or thousands of different revisions of each page and no obvious\r\n way to find the latest version, this isn't very usable...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Tried exploring the restored database using postgres console, to see if we might be able to extract old wiki contents that way - didn't get far with this, not knowing the database structure or much about how to use postgres. Would be easier to explore with something like Navicat, which Alissa could help with (if we want to invest the time).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Created new ''xwiki-old'  Debian 9 VM on 'polaris' host, to try installing older versions of Xwiki (and older postgres), and subsequently updated the VM to Debian 10 to try more versions, but no luck there either. Sadly we don't know what version of xwiki was in use on the original install, so this was a shot in the dark.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Reviewed these failed xwiki restore attempts^ with Kevin &amp;amp; Alissa. Kevin decided to forgo spending more hours on trying to restore the old Xwiki, and instead move forward with a fresh/blank Xwiki install. I went ahead and set it up on the Debian 11 'xwiki' VM I had made earlier:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="http://xwiki.rhinobee.com:8080/xwiki/" target="_blank"&gt;http://xwiki.rhinobee.com:8080/xwiki/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-IR 3/30/22&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1719	7	2022-03-04	4	\N	2022-03-02 12:30:28.325707-08	Kevin	2022-03-30 15:48:03.696899-07	Ian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
