615	3	2	INF-221212 - Mimosa B24 Link from Kenwood.Farm.House to H20 Relay	&lt;p&gt;Kenwood FarmHouse Relay&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9255 Sonoma Hwy&lt;br&gt;Kenwood, CA 95452&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- - - -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;H2O Relay&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9900 Courtney Drive&lt;br&gt;Kenwood, CA 95452&lt;br&gt;_______________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* While checking on Kenwood infrastructure with Julian on 12/8/22 (looking for the cause of recent Bob Maes smokeping alerts), we found B24 BH.AP-Farmhouse-ptp-H2O (10.77.16.50) / BH.ST-H2O-ptp-Farmhouse (10.77.16.40) showing a lot of rate-flux, regularly dipping under 50Mbps capacity in both directions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;* The B24 link RSSI was around -69 dBm, and MRTG doesn't shows any abrupt drops, but gradual decline over time... it used to be in the -50s:&lt;br&gt;https://mrtg1.rhinobee.com/mrtgwork/10.77.16.40-signal.html&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;* Since we know 24GHz has much less tolerance for minor obstructions or misalignment than 5GHz (and B24s don't offer any choice of other channels to try) we figured the most likely causes would be tree growth, misalignment, or a hardware problem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;* For the time being, we've moved traffic off the B24 link, onto the 5GHz Ubnt backup AC.Farmhouse-ptp-H2O (10.77.16.2 &amp;amp; 10.77.16.3), which looks good/stable with 250x250Mbps+ capacity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* I updated the firmware on the B24 pair from v2.5.4 to v2.5.5.5 today (12/12/22), but it didn't help; the low/fluctuating capacity persisted after the upgrade.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-IR 12/12/22&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled Infrastructure&amp;nbsp;Investigation: Mimosa B24 Link Optimization - Tuesday 12.13.2022 @ 9-10AM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Need to investigate the Mimosa B24 link from Kenwood Farmhouse to H2O relay as there have been issues with the link not providing optimal performance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Need to send out rich to the Kenwood Area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-AL 12.12.2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* This morning Rich went out and aligned the B24 on the farmhouse end.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Before the signal was around -70dbm and after alignment we got it to -52dbm which was a massive improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Though after a while Ian pointed out that there were still fluctuations with the capacity Download wasn't as bad but the would dip below 100Mbps and even get as low a 20Mbps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* We sent Rich out to the H2O side though I need to collect his report.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 12/13/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Issue has been resolved, Closing Ticket and transfering notes to Kenwood Farm House Relay Entry in Freeside&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1705	8	2022-12-13	3	\N	2022-12-12 10:46:15.24786-08	Andre	2023-03-08 16:45:50.856648-08	Andre	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
