737	2	2	TT-230222 - William Foss (6475 Starr Road)	&lt;p&gt;William Foss&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6475 Starr Road Starr Road&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windsor, CA&amp;nbsp;95492&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(415) 465-9100&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;bill@331fish.com&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* William called in saying his connection has been all around terrible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Loggin into his CPE and immediatley noticed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. The rates keep jumping between&amp;nbsp;40.5 Mbps / 30 Mbps and&amp;nbsp;30 Mbps / 30 Mbps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. CCQ is jumping between 50-60%.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. The signal is sitting around -74 dbm combined, with a horizontal/vertical of&amp;nbsp;-83 / -74 dBm.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Did a scan and saw hes on frequency 5.17 and there's a CDS device on frequency 5.19 with a strength of -85 and a device with the SSID of "CLUBREP2" on frequency 5.165 with a strength of -82.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Believe it may be interference that is causing issues.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 2/22/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Looked at&amp;nbsp;X1-shiloh-ap(10.77.4.4) and noticed William was not the only customer having poor connections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Changed AP's frequency to 5510 with a control frequency of 5500.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Andre also looked into the AP more and did further optimizing and got everything to look a whole lot better.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Called William and he said he will test everything when he gets home.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* I will close this ticket for now, though if he calls back saying there is still issues I will open a new one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 2/24/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1221	10	2023-02-24	2	\N	2023-02-22 17:28:26.585994-08	Julian	2023-02-28 09:49:48.23802-08	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
916	2	2	TT-230606 - Johan  Lozano - (3915 Mark West Sta Rd, Windsor )	&lt;p&gt;Requested: 06-06-2023 06:30am&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Johan  Lozano&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3915 Mark West Sta Rd&lt;br&gt;Windsor , 95492&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;whs.johan@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;7076949657&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\nDear, Rhino bee\r\n\r\nI am writing to report an issue with my WiFi connection. For the past two days, I have been experiencing difficulties with my internet connection, and my WiFi has not been working at all. I have tried disconnecting and resetting my router several times, but the issue persists.\r\n\r\nI rely on my internet connection for work and other important tasks, and the lack of reliable connectivity has been causing significant inconvenience and frustration. I would appreciate it if you could investigate this issue and provide a solution as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if there are any troubleshooting steps I can take or if you require any further information to resolve the issue. I look forward to hearing back from you soon.\r\n\r\nThank you for your assistance.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\n\r\nJohan Lozano \r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-WC 6/6/2023&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Called and spoke with Johan Lozano, it looks as though his service may have been interrupted by a DFS Event, Andre went in and adjusted the radio frequency of TV west (10.77.2.206) changed to frequency 5630&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-JS 6/6/23&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;	\N	6	2023-06-07	12	\N	2023-06-06 10:59:53.874384-07	\N	2023-06-06 11:28:21.370124-07	Andre	\N	\N	\N	\N	 - 06-06-2023 18:28:06	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
