433	2	2	RMA-  Find the invoice for this device	&lt;p&gt;Hello I need the invoice for this device so I can get it approved for RMA&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;LBE-5AC-Gen2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;MAC -&amp;nbsp;F4:92:BF:44:36:83&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 8/12/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Julian, I need more info: vendor would help.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 8/29/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We got this device from Last Mile Gear.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 9/1/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please verify item #, I did not see anything with this number.&amp;nbsp; There were many PBE 5AC Gen2's purchased in 2 or 5 packs without serial #'s.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 9/8/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The device is a LBE-5AC-Gen2. What you are mentioning is a different product.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 9/8/22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Did not find it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 9/12/22&lt;/p&gt;	\N	10	2022-08-19	2	\N	2022-08-12 12:20:33.775883-07	Julian	2023-03-06 15:48:36.790514-08	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
987	2	2	TT-230808 - Zack  Zimmerman - (5900 Pruitt Ave Ste 110, Windsor)	&lt;p&gt;Requested: 08-08-2023 08:46am&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Zack  Zimmerman&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5900 Pruitt Ave Ste 110&lt;br&gt;Windsor, 95492&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;betty.n@bamcore.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;707-737-0288&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are not able to receive voicemails. Once the phone rings- instead of going to a voicemail, it just hangs up. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-WC 8/8/2023&lt;/p&gt;	\N	6	2023-08-09	12	\N	2023-08-08 12:52:00.633987-07	\N	2023-09-20 17:54:17.242239-07	Andre	\N	\N	\N	\N	 - 08-08-2023 20:07:54	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
748	2	2	TT-230306 - David Rothwell - (7395 Starr Rd, Windsor)	&lt;p&gt;Requested: 03-05-2023 04:08pm&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;David Rothwell&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;7395 Starr Rd&lt;br&gt;Windsor, 95492&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;dave.rothwell@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4083387623&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hi,\r\nI'm having some issues with certain online actions, which I suspect is due to how Rhinobee handles customer Internet traffic.\r\n\r\n1) I am often getting flagged by my work's security team and having my work account locked out due to suspicious looking traffic. They don't give away a lot of info but it sounds like certain use of a VPN or IP hiding mechanism is in place which is triggering the security policy.\r\n\r\n2) I use BitWarden password manager and have noticed then I try to update one of my saved password entries, it blocks me from saving any changes and gives an error saying traffic from my network looks unusual. I suspect this is a similar issue as (1). This doesn't happen when I'm on a different network.\r\n\r\n3) Recently I've tried to buy some concert tickets from axs.com and I get an error page asking if I'm a real fan, stating the following as the reason for the error:\r\nWhy has this happened?\r\nThere are several reason for why this could have occurred, including submitting invalid data, clicking too quickly or using too many devices at the same time.\r\nIP: 216.218.198.232 Request ID: 7a3653110aabcf82\r\nAccess denied\r\nYou do not have access to www.axs.com.\r\n\r\n\r\nIt seems all 3 issues I've observed are likely related. Are there any changes that can be made on Rhinobee's side to make my traffic look more "normal"? I understand with the wireless relays that there are likely several private networks being merged into various links/backhauls and there be not be any fix, but it is quite frustrating when these fairly standard aspects of Internet access are getting blocked.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nDave\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-WC 3/6/2023&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Looked at this ticket with Andre and we believe he may be in need of public IP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Attempted to call him back but he did not answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 3/6/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_______________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Seems I forgot to mark it down but we talked to David about a public IP and he said he was going to think about it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 3/15/23&lt;/p&gt;	2027	10	2023-03-10	12	\N	2023-03-06 13:45:30.607286-08	\N	2023-03-15 11:19:19.923189-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	 - 03-06-2023 21:53:52	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
