811	2	2	AM - 230405 Jackie Moore 10605 Slattery Rd, Glen Ellen, CA 95442  (510) 501-1517  Jackie Cell	&lt;p&gt;Note last payment 4/1/19 when CC failed. Current balance $5510.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4/3/23 Greetings Jacqueline; I am forwarding your message to Andre in sales.&amp;nbsp; He will be able to answer your question about service and usage. Our system shows that it has been used for the past year at your location.&amp;nbsp; I don't understand how it could be used if we picked up our equipment.&amp;nbsp; I will let Andre figure that out. Thank you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On 3/31/2023 6:57 PM, Jacqueline Moore wrote: Hi Linda, I've checked, and I've been paying Hughes Net for monthly internet since I cancelled Rhinobee, I think it was in 2019.&amp;nbsp; (I know it was before the Covid lock-down).&amp;nbsp; At the time I cancelled I spoke with a very nice man at Rhinobee about why I was leaving after having been a customer for quite a few years. I do remember that it took you guys a while to retrieve your equipment from my house, but eventually you did.&amp;nbsp; I am a complete techo-peasant so I don't know what equipment you picked up.&amp;nbsp; I also don't quite understand how people using internet at the house have found themselves on Rhinobee after its service was cancelled, when we have Hughes. So, I'm sorry but I'm not going to pay Rhinobee for services I cancelled when I've been paying another company for the same services.&amp;nbsp; However, I am willing to consider cancelling Hughes and going back to Rhinobee, if its service has gotten better.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;My problem with it was too many users on your system so I couldn't watch movies,it just kept buffering and buffering. I like supporting a local company, so if you could give me some assurance that the service is now good enough to watch movies and how much your monthly charges would be, switching back again is a possibility. Please let me know. Thanks, Jacqueline Moore. The Hughes fees are automatically debited against my charge card.&amp;nbsp; Here's the last one:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; Mar 12, 2023&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;HNS*HughesNet.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; &lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;Bills &amp;amp; utilities, opens menu&amp;nbsp; $136.05&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; &lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;$136.05&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; So, I'm sorry but I'm not going to pay Rhinobee for services I cancelled when I've been paying another company for the same services.&amp;nbsp; However, I am willing to consider cancelling Hughes and going back to Rhinobee, if its service has gotten better.&lt;/p&gt;	1403	8	2023-04-07	9	\N	2023-04-05 10:13:47.656345-07	Linda	2023-05-19 14:29:02.672678-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
