823	2	2	TT-230411 - David Burton (18266 HIGHWAY 128)	&lt;p&gt;David Burton&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;18266 HIGHWAY 128&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Calistoga, CA 94515&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;dburton33@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(415) 710-4706&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* David Burton called in saying he is offline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Was going to see if he is able to power cycle the CPE but he is not at the home.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* I also noticed Dan Dolen who is the head in was fluctuating.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Checked with Dan and will be sending Rich out to check it out&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 4/11/23&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled Service Call: 4/11/23 @ 12PM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Rich arrived and noticed the power setup was changed to be connected to a extension cord that leads to a UPS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Rich connected the power directly to a outlet as he was worried weather may have damaged the ups and or extension cord as it was facing straight up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Checked NSM2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;* Noticed Airmax would blink and rates would fluctuate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;* Added NTP client and put airmax priority to medium.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Did site survery on both ends and didnt see anything causing interfering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Changing frequency on AP from 5240 to 5260(DFS).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* After frequency change everything starting pinging perfectly fine.&lt;/p&gt;	1664	10	2023-04-11	2	\N	2023-04-11 15:36:01.658225-07	Julian	2023-04-11 15:36:01.658225-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
932	2	1	TT-230616 - Kevin Schuh - (505 Wolf Ridge Rd, Glen Ellen)	&lt;p&gt;Requested: 06-15-2023 06:14pm&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kevin Schuh&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;505 Wolf Ridge Rd&lt;br&gt;Glen Ellen, 95422&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;KevinCSchuh@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(415) 710-9121&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;Going out 6/16/2023 *updating wifi *replacing router and adding&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-WC 6/16/2023&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;_________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Service request: 9-10 AM&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** Changing Kilo with Kilo 2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** Updating WiFi&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** Adjusting the radio&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-JS 6/15/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_______________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;ROUTER SWAP:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** Had Rich log into Netonix via cat 5 cable. So when we uploaded the new config he could log into the switch, and stop it from converting back to the old config.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; **Forgot to backup switch config, before we disassembled the Lab. We needed the new switch config to upload to the switch out in the field. Took about 30 min to gain access and backup config. We couldn't access the lab switch from&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Hugh via ssh proxy. After troubleshooting we found that Hugh had a /29 subnet, which did not allow us access to 10.40.4.1. We needed a /24 subnet on Hugh to access the IP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; ** Andre managed to backup the config from Laptop, while we figured out why Hugh couldn't access 10.40.4.1.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Rich installed the dc/dc regulator in anticipation of the APU router board&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Swapped out Kilo (Soekris 6501-70) for the new updated Kilo2 (APU 4D, OpenBSD 7.3)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;** Swap went well with Kilo2. The wireless hosts and access to Kilo2 from the office came back.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; *We checked Nagios and everything was back up and green.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;BH Signal:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** BH.ST-K.Schuh-ptp-BzP.S (10.77.9.29): Signal Strength improved on Thursday, went from -63 dBm to -52 dBm. Which is a 9 dB increase.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; * Kevin Schuh cleared tree/plant growth from in front of the radio on Thursday as per Andres recommendation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; * Rich/Andre decided not to attempt a realignment of the BH to see if they could acquire an even better signal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Schuh LAN:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Upstairs Media Closet&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;: Replaced the airRouter w/&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Unifi Switch ( USW-lite-8-PoE) = 10.0.87.10&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; * Unable to adopt switch&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Unifi AP 6 (U6-Lite-US) = 10.0.87.11&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pantry&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;: Replaced PicoStation M2 w/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Unifi AP 6 (U6-Lite-US) = 10.0.87.12&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**&lt;b style="text-decoration-line: underline;"&gt;Downstairs studio&lt;/b&gt;: Added Unifi AP 6&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Unifi AP 6 (U6-Lite-US) = 10.0.87.13&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; It is wirelessly connecting to&amp;nbsp; Pantry AP&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Install Summary&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**Downloading speeds were improved to 25 to 50 mbps&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**In home Wifi Signal was significantly improved&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;** Rich mentioned Kevin Schuh was very happy with our work&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-JS 6/19/2023&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_______________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Billing:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Waive Labor Costs for the WiFi Job.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(1) Unifi Switch (USW-lite-8-PoE) (@ $120/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$120&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(3) Unifi AP 6 (U6-Lite-US) (@ $150/ea) = &lt;b&gt;$450&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Total = $570&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;AL 6.19.2023&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	\N	6	2023-06-17	12	\N	2023-06-15 18:14:49.558932-07	\N	2023-06-20 09:18:50.411644-07	Andre	\N	\N	\N	\N	 - 06-16-2023 01:24:35	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
778	2	2	AM - 230313 Joseph Barnwell  2401 River Rd, Windsor, CA 95492 jtbarnwell@gmail.com	&lt;p&gt;2/22/23 Greetings Joseph Barnwell, Your statement is attached for the outstanding amount of $2151.&amp;nbsp; There have no payments on your account to date. My instructions are to cancel your service in one week if you do not reply with a payment.&amp;nbsp; I called and there is no answer of your phone. Regards, Linda&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He has not responded.&amp;nbsp; Cancel service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 3/13/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;* Update - Got a Hold of Joseph and he is willing to pay the total amount.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;* Since he's upfront about paying the whole amount we want to take 20% off the total Amount Owing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Owing - $2,406.00&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;20% - $481.20&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Final Amount -&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;$1,924.80&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-AL 4.26.23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Noted&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 4/27/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;__________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;My gut tells me we are being played.&amp;nbsp; He has not paid anything.&amp;nbsp; He was adamant that he had paid when I 1st spoke to him.&amp;nbsp; He said we would send me proof which he never did.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 700;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;I suggest we cancel his service, perhaps that will light a fire under him.&amp;nbsp; If not, no more free service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Collection history:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4/27/23 Left Message To Call to pay balance. (NO REPLY)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2/22/23 Greetings Joseph Barnwell, Your statement is attached for the outstanding amount of $2151.&amp;nbsp; There have no payments on your account to date. My instructions are to cancel your service in one week if you do not reply with a payment.&amp;nbsp; I called and there is no answer of your phone. Regards, (NO REPLY)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2/16/23 Greetings Joseph Barnwell,&amp;nbsp; I'm following up to our conversation of 12/29/22.&amp;nbsp; You were going to call after checking your credit card statements for payments.&amp;nbsp; We have no record of any to date. While we are willing to negotiate a settlement for the balance, we cannot continue to offer free service.Give me a call, let's clear this matter: 707.237.7504.Thank you. (NO REPLY)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;12/29/22 He called concerning payments.&amp;nbsp; I told him we have no record of any since the install 6/30/21.&amp;nbsp; He will call on Monday from his office with his cc payment history.&amp;nbsp; He's certain payments were made.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-LRK 5/10/23&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;__________________________&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;* Joseph barnwell Paid off Debts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;-AL 7.14.2023&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1956	6	2023-04-27	9	\N	2023-03-13 17:09:22.845737-07	Linda	2023-07-14 10:47:36.981114-07	Andre	\N	\N	<li><strong>Accepted</strong> - <span>Willing to pay full amount!</span>Linda 04-27-2023 00:40:26</li>	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
830	2	2	TT-230412 - Johan Lozano (3915 Mark West Station Rd)	&lt;p&gt;Johan Lozano&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;3915 Mark West Station Rd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;Windsor, CA 95492&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;whs.johan@gmail.com&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;707-694-9657&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;______________________________&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Johan left a web contact saying he has been unable to connect.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* I actually left him a message this morning pointing out that his CPE is offline.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Called him back and he explained that he saw lights on the power supply and he attempted to power cycle the radio multiple times.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Scheduled to send Rich out.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;- JD 4/12/23&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;______________________________&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scheduled Service Call: Thursday 4/12/23 @ 11AM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Prepared a PowerBeam M5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;_____________________________&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Rich went in and determined the NanoBridge may be faulty.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Went in and replaced the NanoBridge for a PowerBeam M5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* After we got signal to around -60 dBm and everything is running slowly.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;* Though Rich said he could benefit from having a AC radio.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt;- JD 4/13/23&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;	1380	8	2023-04-13	2	\N	2023-04-12 18:21:28.527021-07	Julian	2023-04-13 12:53:10.322457-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
884	2	2	AM - 230509 Ron Nelson 7374 Shiloh Ridge, Santa Rosa, Ca 95403 (707) 576-7373	&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5/9/23 Greetings Ron: I have cancelled your billing and will alert the support team.&amp;nbsp; They will contact you if there is any of our equipment to pick up.Thank you for your business! Cheers, Linda&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On 5/9/2023 4:19 PM, RON NELSON wrote:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; Hello&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; As you have probably heard the Shiloh Homeowners Assoc put in a fiber optic connection which we are now connected to &amp;amp; no longer need or will be using Rhinobee. Please discontinue service.&amp;nbsp; The wifi was dependable &amp;amp; if we had a loss of service it was quickly &amp;amp; easily fixed. We thank you for providing WiFi to us. Is there any equipment that you would like to have back?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; Thanks Ron &amp;amp; Eileen Nelson&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 05/09/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;_____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We collected our equipment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JD 5/16/23&lt;/p&gt;	1918	6	2023-05-12	9	\N	2023-05-09 16:42:43.924867-07	Linda	2023-05-16 15:29:51.834254-07	Andre	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
831	2	2	TT-230413 - Johan  Lozano - (3915 mark west Sta rd, Windsor )	&lt;p&gt;Requested: 04-12-2023 04:27pm&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Johan  Lozano&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3915 mark west Sta rd&lt;br&gt;Windsor , 95492&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;whs.johan@gmail.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;707-694-9657&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\nIssue with WiFi connection\r\n\r\nDear Rhino bee, \r\n\r\nI am writing to report an issue with my WiFi connection. For the past two days, I have been experiencing difficulties with my internet connection, and my WiFi has not been working at all. I have tried disconnecting and resetting my router several times, but the issue persists.\r\n\r\nI rely on my internet connection for work and other important tasks, and the lack of reliable connectivity has been causing significant inconvenience and frustration. I would appreciate it if you could investigate this issue and provide a solution as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if there are any troubleshooting steps I can take or if you require any further information to resolve the issue. I look forward to hearing back from you soon.\r\n\r\nThank you for your assistance.\r\n\r\nSincerely,\r\nJohan \r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-WC 4/13/2023&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reference ticket #830&lt;/p&gt;	\N	10	2023-04-14	12	\N	2023-04-12 18:22:02.155855-07	\N	2023-04-12 18:22:32.82965-07	Julian	\N	\N	\N	\N	 - 04-13-2023 01:22:32	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
