828	2	2	AM - 230412  Jackie Moore 10605 Slattery Rd, Glen Ellen, CA 95442  (510) 501-1517  Jackie Cell	&lt;p&gt;Collection notes:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5/1/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Greetings Jackie:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I forwarded your request to Andre on our sales team on 4/12/23.&amp;nbsp; I will forward again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hopefully, he will be able to contact you upon your return concerning service.&lt;br&gt;\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thank you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linda&lt;br&gt;\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="moz-cite-prefix"&gt;On 4/28/2023 6:21 PM, Jacqueline Moore wrote:&lt;br&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote type="cite" cite="mid:CACYNdwwB4wB7vULK-V-AnzqNje=2m1KHLN1c83VQLxc9Y3caPw@mail.gmail.com"&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;Hello,&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;Below is where our communication left off, until \r\nrecently when I was sent a bill for this month’s service. &amp;nbsp; As I said \r\nbelow, I’m willing to consider canceling Hughes Net and using your \r\nservice instead, but this hadn’t happened yet because I never heard back\r\n from you&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;&amp;nbsp;I’m traveling next week but will be home by Monday \r\nMay 8th. Please give me a call anytime &amp;nbsp;thereafter to discuss further.&amp;nbsp; \r\nI’m not going to pay for Rhinobee services until and unless we talk and I\r\n cancel Hughes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;I really am sorry for all this confusion.&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n  &lt;div dir="auto"&gt;Jacqueline Moore&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;4/12/23 Sent to Andre Kanga ticket.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4/3/23 Greetings Jacqueline; I am forwarding your message to Andre in sales.&amp;nbsp; He will be able to answer your question about service and usage. Our system shows that it has been used for the past year at your location.&amp;nbsp; I don't understand how it could be used if we picked up our equipment.&amp;nbsp; I will let Andre figure that out. Thank you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On 3/31/2023 6:57 PM, Jacqueline Moore wrote: Hi Linda, I've checked, and I've been paying Hughes Net for monthly internet since I cancelled Rhinobee, I think it was in 2019.&amp;nbsp; (I know it was before the Covid lock-down).&amp;nbsp; At the time I cancelled I spoke with a very nice man at Rhinobee about why I was leaving after having been a customer for quite a few years. I do remember that it took you guys a while to retrieve your equipment from my house, but eventually you did.&amp;nbsp; I am a complete techo-peasant so I don't know what equipment you picked up.&amp;nbsp; I also don't quite understand how people using internet at the house have found themselves on Rhinobee after its service was cancelled, when we have Hughes. So, I'm sorry but I'm not going to pay Rhinobee for services I cancelled when I've been paying another company for the same services.&amp;nbsp; However, I am willing to consider cancelling Hughes and going back to Rhinobee, if its service has gotten better.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;My problem with it was too many users on your system so I couldn't watch movies,it just kept buffering and buffering. I like supporting a local company, so if you could give me some assurance that the service is now good enough to watch movies and how much your monthly charges would be, switching back again is a possibility. Please let me know. Thanks, Jacqueline Moore. The Hughes fees are automatically debited against my charge card.&amp;nbsp; Here's the last one:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; Mar 12, 2023&lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;HNS*HughesNet.com&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; &lt;span style="white-space:pre"&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;Bills &amp;amp; utilities, opens menu&amp;nbsp; $136.05&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; So, I'm sorry but I'm not going to pay Rhinobee for services I cancelled when I've been paying another company for the same services.&amp;nbsp; However, I am willing to consider cancelling Hughes and going back to Rhinobee, if its service has gotten better.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3/27/23 She thinks she had another service during the past 4 years, she will check on her payments and get back to me.&amp;nbsp; She offered to pay $1000, I said we were looking at 1/2 of her $5510 balance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3/27/23 LMTC: Andre verified we are providing service. From Jackie: I’m so sorry for this confusion. I thought you took your routers away a couple of years ago?&amp;nbsp; Or are we still using your services up there?&amp;nbsp; If you are providing internet, of course I want to pay you. Can you give me a call at (510) 501-1517? Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3/20/23 Greetings Jackie Moore, Your statement is attached for $5360.&amp;nbsp; We have not received a payment since April 1, 2019. We are willing to negotiate a settlement as I mentioned in the phone message I left on March 16, 2023.We must hear from you by Thursday, March 23, 2023.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Otherwise your service will be canceled. Respectfully,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3/16/23 Spoke to daughter Alicia, got her correct email.&amp;nbsp; Bills have been going to wrong address.&amp;nbsp; LMTC for Jackie concerning balance to call to neg. settlement of acct over $5K.&amp;nbsp; Told her it need to be resolved, we can no longer offer free internet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Other Contact: Scott Schoepflin sschoepflin@divcowest.com (415) 284-5731&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Alicia Dantzker, daughter&amp;nbsp; adantzker@gmail.com 510-507-1517&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;8/31/22 Sent billing update letter and statement:&amp;nbsp; Greetings Jackie Moore, This is our second request.&amp;nbsp; Your statement is attached.&amp;nbsp; Please remit payment for your outstanding balance of $4310.&amp;nbsp; We can schedule arrangements. Thx&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-LRK 4/12/23&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;looking at QBO, ALL w/o thru 6/2023 (she paid Hughes during the time Rhinobee was billing her and she refuses to pay Rhinobee PAST due amounts) but she has come back to Rhinobee, effective 7/1/2023.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;LM 10.10.23&lt;/p&gt;	1403	6	2023-04-14	9	\N	2023-04-12 11:15:27.759514-07	Linda	2023-10-10 13:35:32.564575-07	Laura	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
